    Bug 1945961 - Do not skip deleted messages when reporting message events. r=aleca

    When emitting message events, for example onMoved or onDeleted, some
    messages can already be gone when they are about to be converted for
    reporting. We solved this by using a cache. On IMAP, messages can be
    marked as deleted, which is stored in its (cached) flags.

    Since Bug 1881929 the conversion step skips (cached) messages which
    have these flags set. This caused intermittent fails, if the IMAP
    mark-as-deleted flag was already set before the message was chached.
    Such messages are then skipped in the conversion step and not reported.

    To finally solve this, this patch adds an option to the reporting
    MessageList to disable skipping of IMAP marked-as-deleted messages for
    all message events.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D236800

